hifiberry-sendspin (0.1.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Extension icon: use sendspin's own icon, now carried by
    hifiberry-webui 0.21.9 so it resolves before the extension is
    installed. The generic stand-ins were both wrong: music.svg rendered
    too thin (115-unit viewBox against the set's 23) and
    music-note-simple-light.svg too heavy (a fill-designed silhouette
    stroked with fill:none traces the outline of the outline).

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 12:15:00 +0000

hifiberry-sendspin (0.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Extension icon: use music-note-simple-light.svg instead of music.svg.
    music.svg is drawn on a 115-unit viewBox where every other icon uses
    23, so at the same stroke-width its lines came out five times thinner
    and rendered as a pale grey smudge next to the other extension cards.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-sendspin (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Publish as a HiFiBerry extension: declare the XB-Extension metadata so
    the package appears in the web interface's extension catalog. Removed
    from the hbos-full bundle, which now installs it on demand instead.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-sendspin (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * postinst: restart config-server when it is running so a post-boot install
    (e.g. via hbos-full) is picked up and the WebUI can start the player. Fixes
    "can't be started in the UI" after apt-installing onto a running system.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Wed, 08 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-sendspin (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: Sendspin player daemon for Music Assistant.
    - player/controller/metadata roles via sendspin-cpp
    - ALSA default-device output; ALSA mixer volume (both directions)
    - pushes now-playing metadata + cover art to audiocontrol
    - reports the audio stream format (codec/sample rate/bit depth) to
      audiocontrol
    - transport command endpoint (127.0.0.1:3547) and mDNS advertisement

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Wed, 08 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
